Package: codrug
Version: @VERSION@
Section: science
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-venv, python3-pip
Recommends: python3.10, rsync
Maintainer: Moisés Maia <moimaian@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Homepage: https://github.com/moimaian/CODRUG
Description: QSAR analysis and machine learning tool for drug discovery
 CODRUG is a PyQt5-based graphical tool for QSAR analysis using machine
 learning models: preparation of labeled internal datasets, preprocessing,
 exploratory and statistical analysis, generation of molecular descriptors
 and feature engineering, construction and validation of regression,
 classification and clustering models, cross-validation, hyperparameter
 optimization, and prediction of classes or bioactivities in external
 databases.
 .
 This package installs the application files to /opt/codrug and a menu
 launcher. On first run, CODRUG itself creates an isolated Python 3.10
 virtual environment at ~/.venv/CODRUG and installs its own scientific
 dependencies (RDKit, scikit-learn, PyCaret, etc.) into it — this package
 does not do that as root during installation, by design (see
 packaging/deb/README.md).
